The installer (and `make diarization-model` / `make rnnoise-model`) downloads
the third-party model files below. They are used unmodified and are not part
of the stt-faster source.

1. pyannote speaker-diarization-community-1
   Authors:  pyannote (Hervé Bredin), pyannoteAI
   Licence:  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0)
             https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
   Source:   https://huggingface.co/pyannote-community/speaker-diarization-community-1
             revision 8a527374977391da736e0daaef26855d949d9685
             (ungated mirror of pyannote/speaker-diarization-community-1)
   Files:    config.yaml, README.md, segmentation/, embedding/, plda/, unmodified.
             The model card (README.md) is kept beside the weights.
   Parts:    segmentation/  pyannote segmentation (Alexis Plaquet, Hervé Bredin)
             embedding/     WeSpeaker ResNet34-LM (Hongji Wang et al., WeNet),
                            via pyannote/wespeaker-voxceleb-resnet34-LM
             plda/          PLDA model and x-vector transform trained by
                            BUT Speech@FIT for VBx (Federico Landini, Ján Profant,
                            Mireia Diez, Lukáš Burget),
                            https://github.com/BUTSpeechFIT/VBx

2. RNNoise model sh.rnnn (somnolent-hogwash)
   Author:   Gregor Richards
   Source:   https://github.com/GregorR/rnnoise-models
             commit 3eee541a283fd3b8f81b85b1748e3b9ccbefa04d,
             somnolent-hogwash-2018-09-01/sh.rnnn, unmodified.
